+| Change | Effect (Qwen3.8-27B Q8_0, four dies) | Switch |
+|---|---|---|
+| MMVQ 16-column width + gfx906 launch knobs + Q8_0 fast path | decode +9 / +62 / +34% at 8 / 12 / 16 slots on the split, +31% at 8 slots on one die | compile-time knobs in `mmvq.cu` |
+| Fused RMS_NORM+MUL emits the Q8_1 copy into the q8_1 cache | exact; 0% (kept for the launch count) | `GGML_CUDA_NORM_Q8=0` |
+| Residual ADD inside the fused norm kernel | exact; +1.6% single stream | `GGML_CUDA_ADD_NORM=0` |
+| Delta-net producers (q/k norm, beta sigmoid) folded into the GDN kernel | +1.8% single stream, bit-exact reduction order; decode batches only | `GGML_CUDA_GDN_PREFUSE=0` (bitmask 1/2/4) |
+| `GGML_TP_AR_MAX_NE` explicit size gate for the custom allreduce | with `=20481` (4 rows): single stream +14.5%, 2 slots +19%, 8+ unchanged | env |
+| One-column whole-block (vdr 8) MMVQ load | +2.8% single stream on the split, +7.1% on one die | compile-time |
+
+Combined on the 2026-09-07 fork base: single stream 48 → 58 tok/s, one die 20.4 → 21.7, 8–32 slots unchanged, prefill unchanged,
+perplexity identical (`llama.cpp-benchmarking/reports/2026-09-08-next-steps-measurements.md`). The same series on this branch is
+validated by `qwen38-27b-gfx906-master-validate.md` in the benchmarking folder.
+
+## Build and run
+
+```sh
+scripts/gfx906/build.sh /opt/llama.cpp-gfx906        # cmake flags every measurement used
+set -a; . scripts/gfx906/env.sh; set +a                # RCCL topology, custom allreduce with the 4-row gate
+LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/llama.cpp-gfx906/lib /opt/llama.cpp-gfx906/bin/llama-server -m model.gguf \
+  --device rocm0,rocm1,rocm2,rocm3 -sm tensor -fa on -b 2048 -ub 2048 -np 16 -c 524288
+```
+
+The binaries carry no rpath: always set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` to the install's `lib/`. Profiles, the optimiser and the power rules
+are in the companion tuning guide (`llama.cpp-benchmarking/`, `settings/launch.sh`).
+
+## Keeping up with upstream
+
+```sh
+git fetch upstream && git checkout master && git merge --ff-only upstream/master && git push origin master
+git checkout gfx906 && git merge master            # resolve; the fork's files are ggml-backend-meta.cpp, ggml-cuda/*, src/models/*
+scripts/gfx906/build.sh /opt/llama.cpp-gfx906-candidate
+# validate before promoting: test-backend-ops (MUL_MAT, MUL_MAT_ID, RMS_NORM, GATED_DELTA_NET), perplexity 16K (5.5969 on
+# Qwen3.8-27B Q8_0), greedy + KL at 64-token batches against the current production, llama-bench pp2048/tg128 on tp4 and one die,
+# batched-bench 1..17,24,32 slots  ->  llama.cpp-benchmarking/tools/gfx906-master-validate.sh
+```
+
+Also fetch the mx-llama.cpp fork (`git fetch mxxm --tags`) and merge its newer tags when they carry gfx906 work; its features
+are documented in `FEATURES.md`, and its author rebases onto upstream every few days.
